=== FILE: components/protocols/add-paper.md ===
---
name: add-paper
trigger: "add paper"
aliases:
  - "save paper"
  - "capture paper"
  - "queue paper"
---

## What this protocol does

Capture a paper into the workspace from a URL / DOI / arXiv ID / local PDF reference. Creates a structured markdown file under papers/ with frontmatter (title, authors, year, source, status=queued) and a notes block.

## Steps

1. Ask the user for the paper reference: URL / DOI / arXiv ID / file path / freeform citation
2. Ask for a short take or 1-2 sentence reason it caught their interest (optional but recommended)
3. Derive a slug from the title (lowercase, kebab-case, max 60 chars)
4. Create papers/<slug>.md with the canonical paper frontmatter and the user's note
5. Update the paper-inbox artifact (status: queued)
6. Confirm with the user, naming the created file and its inbox status

## Config values used

- `{{config.install_dir}}` — Installation directory
- `{{config.workspace_dir}}` — Research workspace directory
- `{{config.author_name}}` — Your name
- `{{config.default_review_template}}` — Default review template
- `{{config.pdf_viewer_hint}}` — PDF viewer (optional)

